Generated runtime exception
---------------------------

The Xen-owned runtime machine code that this compiler emits or embeds in
generated user executables, including code emitted by the experimental JIT,
is additionally available under your choice of MIT OR Apache-2.0.
This additional permission applies only to that runtime code as included in
compiler output. It does not relicense the compiler's source, compiler
executable, or verification infrastructure under MIT.

Compiling your own source with Xen does not change the license of your
source. For Xen-owned runtime code included in redistributed executables,
retain the applicable MIT copyright and permission notice or comply with
the Apache-2.0 terms, according to your choice. The standard library and
examples use the repository's default dual license.

Individual SPDX notices and third-party notices must be preserved.
